On 2007-10-01, Philip Potter <pgp@see.sig.invalid> wrote:
> Derek Ray wrote:
>> I'm seriously considering having a "missile launcher slot" for your
>> player to automatically switch to, much like a)pplying a polearm
>> automatically wields it.  (You'd have to unwield it manually.)  This
>> doesn't sound like much but if it removes a tiny bit of tedium WRT using
>> ranged launchers, perhaps it would be good.
>
> How about when you attempt to fire an arrow and you already have a bow 
> in your inventory, you automatically wield it?
>
> I see two complications with this approach:
> 1) Which bow to select when you have multiple bows?
> 2) What if you have an unid'd cursed bow as your only bow?

Yep.  Those are both showstoppers, really.

> The solution I propose to these is for the autobow feature to only work 
> when exactly one appropriate buc'd launcher and never to autowield an 
> unbuc'd launcher.

That's kinda bad, really.  If you accidentally pick up a bow, suddenly
your autobow feature no longer works?  :/  You might be carrying
multiple launchers on purpose, for example -- ie. taking an elven bow to
be BUC ID'ed so you can match up to elven arrows, while using a known +0 
ordinary bow in the meantime.  And you might not _have_ a bag.

> It's a bit ugly, but so is providing another equipment slot. I'm not 
> sure which idea I prefer. :/

Providing another slot like Q)uiver does is a better solution.  Once you 
have another slot available, you can have it prompt you for which bow to 
use if none is in the slot.  (You don't want it to autograb if there's only
one because of the cursed-items chance; the player should have to make
that mistake directly on his own, not indirectly.  Quivering cursed
arrows doesn't have the same penalty, so.)

After all, once you have a launcher, you generally are deciding to
'specialize' in that type of ranged weapon.  You won't switch out
launchers anywhere near as often as you'll switch out ammo.
 
